FishEye

FishEye is a software tool developed at the California Institute of Technology
to assist ecologists, fisheries scientists, and other users with sonar-based
salmon counting and related ecological analysis.

Funding

FishEye was developed at the California Institute of Technology with support
from the Resnick Sustainability Institute.

Attribution and Citation

If you use FishEye in academic, scientific, conservation, management, or other
published work, we request that you cite or acknowledge the FishEye project
and its contributors.

Citation details are provided in the repository's `CITATION.cff` file and/or
README.

